/**
\fn pdg::Scene::raycast(Point start, Point end, CollisionQueryOptions options)
\brief Return the closest accepted segment entry hit, or null.
Queries inspect current authoritative scene geometry before stepping and while
paused, independently of cameras, render interpolation, visibility, input and
collision-response switches. Enabled attached Sprite, Part and Particle colliders
are eligible, including bodyless colliders. Basic and Chipmunk configurations use
the same geometry algorithms. Touching counts and a zero-length ray tests containment.

Call outside scene update/draw traversal. Queries during advance(), including timer
and contact callbacks, and recursive queries from predicates throw. Predicates must
not mutate geometry, scene membership or results, advance scenes, or dispose scenes
or layers. Predicate errors propagate and leave the reused array empty.

The scene reuses one array and a pool of hit records, including their Point and
Vector fields. All returned arrays and hits are valid until the next query on that
scene or disposal. This includes single-hit queries. Copy fields and coordinates
when keeping a result; copying the array alone does not copy its hit records.
Queries on another scene do not invalidate these results. Treat returned arrays,
records and coordinates as read-only. Disposal empties the array and clears its
collider references. Hit records retain colliders while active; shape IDs may cease
to exist after geometry changes.

\htmlonly[block]
<div class="shared-api-options">
\endhtmlonly
\anchor scene_collision_query_options
\par Shared query options

| Field | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| maxHits | 16 | Overlap limit, integer 0 to 1048576; zero returns an empty array. Cast array overloads take maxHits as a separate parameter. |
| layerMask | 4294967295 | Unsigned 32-bit mask intersecting layer queryBits. Zero selects none. Layers default to bit 1. |
| layers | All scene layers | Optional SpriteLayer array intersected with layerMask. Empty selects none; foreign/detached layers throw. |
| categoryMask | 4294967295 | Unsigned 32-bit mask intersecting collider categories. |
| includeSensors | true | Include sensor colliders. |
| excludedColliders | Empty | Collider identities to exclude. |
| excludedBodies | Empty | PhysicsBody identities whose colliders are excluded. |
| predicate | None | Synchronous boolean function(collider), called once per eligible collider before limiting results. |

\anchor scene_collision_query_hit
\par CollisionQueryHit fields

| Field | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| collider, shapeId | Collider and public shape identity. |
| point | Cast target point or nearest point on filled geometry. Initial overlaps can return an interior point. |
| normal | Outward normal toward the query; zero for initial overlaps and nearest points inside a shape. |
| fraction | Cast travel fraction in [0,1]. |
| distance | Cast travel distance or nearest filled-geometry distance in world units. |
| initialOverlap | Cast starts touching/overlapping; distance and fraction are zero. |

Overlap results expose identity only; other fields are zero. Array overloads of raycast(start, end, maxHits, options) and
sweepCircle(center, radius, delta, maxHits, options), and overlap methods,
return at most maxHits entries, sorted by distance, collider ID and shape ID.
Overlaps use identity ordering. Decomposition pieces do not duplicate a public
shape hit. Arrays have exactly the stored hit count; a miss returns an empty array.
No truncation flag is exposed. Circle sweeps translate against current stationary
geometry; nonuniform scale/shear uses the existing curved-boundary approximation.
Layer queryBits are runtime settings and are not serialized in layer snapshots.
Finite coordinates and nonnegative finite radii/distances are required. Boxes must
have positive dimensions. Invalid requests throw.
\htmlonly[block]
</div>
\endhtmlonly

Storage is reused after warming up to the requested capacity. Geometry snapshots,
candidate collection, script/native argument transport and sorting may still
allocate; the API does not promise allocation-free queries.

\param start Scene world-space segment start.
\param end Scene world-space segment end.
\param options Optional selection; see \ref scene_collision_query_options.
\return Closest accepted CollisionQueryHit, or null. The hit is reused on the next query.
\note Attach searched layers to a live scene; no physics step is required.
\par Example
\code{.js}
const game = new pdg.Scene();
const terrain = game.createSpriteLayer();
terrain.createSprite().setupCollider().setBox(new pdg.Rect(100, 0, 120, 100));
const hit = game.raycast(new pdg.Point(0, 50), new pdg.Point(200, 50));
if (hit) console.log(hit.distance); // 100 world units
const hits = game.overlapCircle(new pdg.Point(110, 50), 20, {maxHits: 8});
for (const entry of hits) console.log(entry.shapeId);
// Keep a copy before another query reuses entry and its coordinate objects.
const saved = hits.map(entry => ({collider: entry.collider, shapeId: entry.shapeId}));
game.dispose();
\endcode
*/
/**
\fn pdg::Scene::raycast(Point start, Point end, uint maxHits, CollisionQueryOptions options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry using shared result storage.
\param start Segment start.
\param end Segment end.
\param maxHits Integer limit 0 to 1048576; zero returns an empty array.
\param options Optional selection; see \ref scene_collision_query_options.
\return CollisionQueryHit[] with at most maxHits entries; empty on a miss. Valid until the next query on this scene or disposal.
*/
/**
\fn pdg::Scene::sweepCircle(Point center, number radius, Vector delta, CollisionQueryOptions options)
\brief Query matching scene geometry using shared result storage.
\param center Initial world center.
\param radius Finite nonnegative world radius.
\param delta World translation.
\param options Optional selection; see \ref scene_collision_query_options.
\return Closest hit or null. Valid until the next query on this scene or disposal.
*/
/**
\fn pdg::Scene::sweepCircle(Point center, number radius, Vector delta, uint maxHits, CollisionQueryOptions options)
